# Frontend — official shadcn/ui

## Source of truth

- Registry: https://ui.shadcn.com/
- Project config: `frontend/components.json` (style `new-york`, CSS variables, zinc base).
- **Always** install with the official CLI, then import. Never re-implement a “similar” button/sidebar/login/calendar.

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add <component-or-block>
```

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
import { SidebarProvider } from "@/components/ui/sidebar"

// ❌ BAD — custom twin of shadcn
export function PrettyButton() { return <button className="rounded-md bg-primary..." /> }
```

## Required blocks

| Surface | Command |
|---------|---------|
| Login | `npx shadcn@latest add login-04` |
| Admin shell | `npx shadcn@latest add sidebar-07` |

Keep generated block files under `frontend/src/components/` (e.g. `login-04/`, `sidebar-07/`) and wire pages to them.

## Dark / light + accents

- Use official **next-themes** + shadcn CSS variables (`--background`, `--primary`, …).
- Accent palette via `data-accent` (and shared helpers). Every colored surface must use semantic tokens / accent vars — no raw `#hex` for brand UI.
- Toggle light/dark with the official theme helper pattern already in `AppProviders` / toolbar — do not invent a parallel theme system.

## Date picker

- Base control: official shadcn Calendar + Popover (`npx shadcn@latest add calendar popover`).
- Locale layer on top: Jalali UI when `fa`, Gregorian when `en` (see i18n rule). Do not replace the shadcn calendar with an unrelated custom widget without the official base.

## Responsive

- Mobile-first. Sidebar uses sheet/collapsible patterns from sidebar-07 on small screens.
- Verify layouts at common breakpoints before considering a UI task done.
